{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/closing-the-loop/SKILL.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:08:04.667990Z","id":"dbca17401ea92caac5c7d17339b9fee6fcaf3f930b09a26ed7d05efbdfe2cae7","body":{"detail":"Verified with the 0.8.0 binary: after recording a span annotation and then shortening the file so the span no longer exists, `qualifier review --format json` reports `{\"status\":\"missing\",\"detail\":{\"reason\":\"span lines 3..=3 beyond file length\"}}` — a status distinct from `drifted`, per src/cli/commands/freshness.rs's `FreshnessStatus::Missing` branch. Step 3's text only says 'For each `drifted` location, find its record ... Re-anchor it on the new lines with `--supersedes`'; a `missing` annotation cannot be re-anchored the same way (there is no new span to point at), and the step never mentions the status or what to do about it, so an agent following the checklist literally has no instruction for annotations `qualifier review` reports as missing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":39},"content_hash":"fbaf13da1a1150b02502723d9118a654418ecd67be4fb5219d3146d70aa70b32"},"suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to step 3 covering `missing` results, e.g. surface them to the user rather than re-anchoring, since the span or file is gone rather than merely changed.","summary":"closing-the-loop step 3 ('Drift') only handles `qualifier review`'s `drifted` status; it gives no guidance for `missing`","tags":["review","review:claude-plugin-pr14","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/closing-the-loop/SKILL.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:17:14.839527Z","id":"c6601122d64efb6f48e533482e869245ea0230780601fb4dba6681d564cf6e71","body":{"detail":"plugins/claude-code/skills/closing-the-loop/SKILL.md:21-37 (step 3, Drift) says 'For each `drifted` location ...' and gives only the re-anchor-with---supersedes procedure. The word 'missing' does not appear anywhere in the file. src/cli/commands/freshness.rs:131 and :161-162 emit a separate 'missing' status, with a 'reason' detail, from FreshnessStatus::Missing. That status has no new span to re-anchor to, so the checklist leaves those results unhandled.","kind":"comment","references":"dbca17401ea92caac5c7d17339b9fee6fcaf3f930b09a26ed7d05efbdfe2cae7","summary":"confirmed: step 3 covers only `drifted` and gives no instruction for `missing`","tags":["verified","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/closing-the-loop/SKILL.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T17:00:14.408869Z","id":"9604380b6e91dfc8c011efb1e2109d37396711d3268cab60b963fdab2dde8fc6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6a733e989f42ba0d270a61225768f5959841d00f","summary":"step 3 now documents a `missing` result (file not found or span past EOF) alongside `drifted`, with moved-within-file, moved-to-another-file, and deleted handling (SKILL.md:38-44); scripts/test-plugin.sh ok: closing-the-loop step 3 covers drifted and missing review results","supersedes":"dbca17401ea92caac5c7d17339b9fee6fcaf3f930b09a26ed7d05efbdfe2cae7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
